==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|grc}} {{term|πανοπλία|tr=panoplía|lang=grc}}, from {{term|πάν||all|tr=pan|lang=grc}}+ {{term|ὅπλον||[[arms]]|tr=oplos|lang=grc}}.

Cognate to {{fr}} {{term|panoplie|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpæ.nə.ˌpliː/}}
* {{audio|en-us-panoply.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|panoplies}}

# A [[splendid]] [[display]] of something.
#* '''1961''', J. A. Philip,  "Mimesis in the ''Sophistês'' of Plato," ''Transactions and Proceedings of the American Philological Association'', vol. 92, p. 459,
#*: Even though we cannot affirm that the products of mimesis are invested in the '''panoply''' of existence.
# {{context|by extension}} a collection or display of weaponry
# [[ceremonial|Ceremonial]] [[garment]]s, complete with all [[accessories]].
# A complete set of [[armour]].
# {{context|by extension}} Something that [[cover]]s and [[protect]]s.

